    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Initially, sinus rhythm is recorded with a heart rate of 70 bpm.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "First, the operative field (puncture site) was treated with betadine and alcohol. Then, under local anesthesia with Sol. Novocaini 0.5% - 20.0 ml, the right femoral vein was punctured twice using the Seldinger technique with a needle, through which 2 electrodes were introduced into the heart cavity for performing electrophysiological study (EFS) in the positions of CS and His.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "Title",
      "text": "Sinus rhythm electrophysiological study (EPS) conducted:",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "(Heart rate 170 bpm) typical with AVNRT.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Using a mapping-ablation electrode in LAO=30°, modification of AV nodal conduction was performed: 3 effective applications were carried out in the right mid-septal area with parameters: P = 30-40 W; t = 50-55°C; I = 95-110 Ohm and a duration of 60 seconds, during which a slow rhythm from the AV junction was recorded.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "Title",
      "text": "Further, an electrophysiological study (EPS) was performed:",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Wenckebach retrograde point = 140 bpm.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Antegrade Wenckebach point = 190 bpm.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "Title",
      "text": "Subsequently, Atropine 0.1%-0.5 ml was administered and a control electrophysiological study (EFS) was conducted:",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Wenckebach retrograde point = 160 bpm.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "RERP AVU = 280(120) msec.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Antegrade Wenckebach point = 220 bpm.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "AERP AVU = 200(120) msec.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "Conduction through the His-Purkinje system. Tachycardia is not induced by frequent and programmed stimulation methods.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "element_type": "NarrativeText",
      "text": "The procedure was completed. Decannulation. Hemostasis. Aseptic stickers on the puncture sites. The patient was transferred to the department in sinus rhythm.",
      "metadata": {
        "filename": "АВУРТ.pdf",
        "filetype": "application/pdf",
        "last_modified": "2026-02-17T11:50:20",
        "page_number": 1
      }
    },
